  "math_readback": [
    {
      "claim": "bridge gap >9005",
      "argument": "Existing improvedEnvelope>90 plus pi-upper square and pi-lower bounds gives pi(x/e)-pi(x)^2*log(x)/(e*x)>90. Since x>1 and e*x>0, gap>90*e*x/log(x). On[1.49e12,1e19], log(x)<=44,e*x>=x, so9005*log(x)<90*e*x. No endpoint numerical result is newly assumed."
    },
    {
      "claim": "height40 expression >9005",
      "argument": "For x>=exp40, L=log(x)>=40. exp Taylor term8 gives L^8<=40320*x; L^2>=1600 yields L^6<=26*x. Also x>=1e9, so (37/200)*x^2>9005*26*x>=9005*L^6. The strict QRH actual-gap theorem supplies the next inequality under the existing assumptions."
    },
    {
      "claim": "source allowance unchanged",
      "argument": "The original upperPi is li+3-(1/20)*sqrt(x)/log(x). The existing Buthe lower input at x/e has L-1>=27; its coefficient39/20+(39/10)/27+(39/2)/27^2=10309/4860 is below1061/500 with exact slack49/60750. The new margin theorem reuses this source-correct allowance and adds no literature premise or formula modification."
    },
    {
      "claim": "actual pi and endpoint coverage",
      "argument": "Both final declarations concern RamanujanPV.gap, defined using IEANTN.primeCounting(x)=Nat.primeCounting(floor_nat(x)). The analytic split is closed at1e19 on the bridge and open above it on the height40 argument. Finite source coverage is[N0,1490000000001), while the analytic ray begins at1490000000000, giving a one-unit overlap and no gap."
    },
    {
      "claim": "global result remains conditional",
      "argument": "SourceGlobalAssembly explicitly consumes SourceMarginCertificate N0 1490000000001 9005 rows AND every original row pair of actual QuotientCCell.SourceExecution((next-1),P) and SourceExecution(j,Q). These source count objects include input range/capacity/owned buffers and a linked actual counter Run; source_execution_count derives exact Nat prime counts. Existence for all full-range outputs is not asserted by this theorem."
    }
